Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 02:50:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(bills,reports): finish pending-bill approval (G-19
 #893); clamp share bars to [0,100] (#909)

G-19: BillModal re-applied the 5,000 submission threshold when a reviewer
approved an already-pending bill, forcing status back to 'pending' forever, so
an approval could never complete. The threshold now only gates new/draft
submissions; reviewing a pending bill finishes the decision. Adds a regression
test under the existing G-19 scenario.

#909: the decorative share bars in Income-by-source and Expense-by-category only
upper-bounded width, so a negative share produced an invalid negative CSS width
that browsers reject (the block fell back to auto and filled the track). Negative
shares now render an empty track; >100% still fills one track. Text, share and
CSV stay signed. New test src/tests/share-bar-clamp.test.tsx with hand-worked
books (net 10,445 / 25,335 cents) covering both components.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
